Description:
   Creates or extends the sponsors.yml file of an event, or of a series with --series-level.

   Each sponsor is given as slug_or_name|tier|badge, in a series' file as slug_or_name|tier|badge|from|to.
   Everything after slug_or_name is optional. slug_or_name is exactly the slug, an alias slug, the name, an
   alias name or an alternate name of an organization in data/organizations.yml. If any of them isn't there,
   nothing is written: add the organization with bin/rails g organization first.

   A new file gets the tiers of --tiers, or else the tiers of the sponsors in the order they first appear,
   highest first. Tiers can only be added on the first pass. A new sponsor's tier defaults to "Sponsors".
   A sponsor already in the file is updated and keeps what isn't given, its tier included (in a series' file:
   the entry starting in the same period).

Example: Create the sponsors.yml file of an event with all its sponsors
    bin/rails g sponsors --event rails-world-2026 --sponsors \
      "appsignal|Platinum" "typesense|Gold|Wifi Sponsor" "Planet Argon|Gold" "shopify|Silver"

    This will create:
        data/rails-world/rails-world-2026/sponsors.yml
    with the tiers Platinum, Gold and Silver.

Example: Add a sponsor to an existing sponsors.yml file, or change its tier or badge
  bin/rails g sponsors --event tropical-on-rails-2026 --sponsors "appsignal|Platinum|Wifi Sponsor"

Example: A meetup group's sponsors over the years
  bin/rails g sponsors --event-series lrug --series-level --sponsors "gocardless|Sponsors||2015|2019" "cleo|Sponsors||2020"
